// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  msx2_ui_strings.def -- the interface words, kept out of the code banks
//
//  The duel screen and the story screens are compiled into cartridge segment 2,
//  a hard 16 KB that was full.  Their string literals were 1.6 KB of it: a
//  whole feature worth of code sitting in the tightest budget the port has,
//  while the cartridge around it has megabytes of room for text.  So the words
//  live in the TEXT segment with the card names, at a fixed stride, and a
//  screen asks for one by id -- Msx2_UiText(MSX2_S_SUMMON).
//
//  tools/msx2/gen_msx_scenes.py parses this file, packs the strings and writes
//  the ids into src/generated/msx2_scenes.h.  Add a line here and use the id;
//  nothing else has to change.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
